5:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The Facebook-to-Landing-Page Transition Shock"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Facebook and Instagram are passive scroll environments. People are not there to evaluate products. They're looking at photos of people they know, watching short videos, or following a news thread. When your ad interrupts that experience, you've created a pattern-break - and if it's compelling enough, they click."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"That click is a sudden context switch from entertainment to evaluation. The visitor goes from a warm, familiar social feed to a completely unfamiliar landing page. They're now in a different mental mode. They're asking: what is this, can I trust it, is this worth my time? You have approximately three seconds to answer those questions before they hit the back button and return to the scroll."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Most landing pages fail this test not because they're badly designed in isolation, but because they don't account for the emotional state the visitor arrived in. The page must catch that state and sustain it - not reset it. The gap between where the ad left the visitor and where the page picks them up is where most Meta ad spend goes to die."}]]}]
6:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The Message Match Problem on Meta"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Meta ads work by pattern-breaking the feed. A strong ad creates a specific tone, makes a specific promise, and shows a specific visual style. The visitor clicked because something in that combination resonated. When they arrive on the landing page, they're looking - consciously or not - for confirmation that they're in the right place."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Message match is the degree of continuity between the ad and the landing page. It's not just about repeating the same headline - it's about maintaining the same tone, visual energy, and implied promise. A warm, conversational video ad that lands on a cold, corporate-looking page creates immediate dissonance. The visitor's subconscious registers a mismatch and the trust that the ad had built evaporates."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The practical fix is to design your landing page and your ad as a single unit. Use the same imagery style. Echo the ad's headline in the page's H1. If the ad is casual and direct, the page must be casual and direct. If the ad showed a specific outcome ('Stop losing leads to your landing page'), the page should lead with that same outcome - not a generic brand statement. Continuity is trust."}]]}]
7:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The Trust Gap: Meta Traffic Is Cold"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"There's a fundamental difference between Google search traffic and Meta traffic that most advertisers underestimate. Google visitors have declared intent - they typed a query that tells you exactly what they're looking for. Meta visitors have done no such thing. They were living their lives and your ad interrupted them. They have no prior relationship with your brand and no expressed need."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"This means a page designed for warm or high-intent traffic may need a different proof sequence for Meta visitors. If the page assumes brand familiarity, compare engagement before and after specific, attributable proof rather than assuming that proof volume alone determines the result."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The minimum proof floor for a Meta landing page is: at least one or two testimonials visible above the fold, a real face or person in the first screen (anonymised corporate stock photography actively reduces trust), and recognisable logos or credentials if your market responds to authority signals. These elements don't need to be elaborate - a name, a photo, and a specific result is enough - but they need to be present before the visitor reaches any form or CTA."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The goal is to compress the trust-building timeline. In a normal sales process, trust develops over multiple touchpoints. On a landing page, you have one shot. Front-load the evidence."}]]}]
8:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Lead Forms vs Landing Pages: Choosing the Right Friction"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Meta's native Lead Ads - where the form lives inside Facebook rather than on a separate landing page - are worth understanding before assuming your landing page is the right tool. Lead Forms reduce interaction steps by pre-filling profile data. Compare both lead volume and downstream qualification in your own funnel; the form location alone does not establish quality."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A dedicated landing page adds steps - the visitor has to click through, wait for a page to load, and read before acting. Those steps may filter intent or may simply add abandonment. Use qualified-lead and downstream sales data to distinguish the two."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Neither approach is universally correct. The question is what your follow-up process can handle. Compare the two paths on the same definitions for qualified lead, response, and sale, then choose the friction level your process can support."}]]}]
9:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Diagnosing the Leak: Is the Ad Working or Is the Page Failing?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Before you change your landing page, confirm that it is actually the leak. Meta's ad analytics give you the data to make this call precisely, and acting on the wrong diagnosis is expensive."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The diagnostic split is straightforward. Click-through rate (CTR) measures whether the ad is compelling enough to interrupt the scroll. Conversion rate (CVR) measures whether the landing page converts the interest the ad created. These are separate problems with separate fixes."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"CTR above 1%, CVR below 1%:"}]," The ad is working. People are interested enough to click. The landing page is the leak - it's failing to maintain the state the ad created."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"CTR below 0.5%:"}]," The ad creative needs attention before the landing page. Low CTR means the interruption isn't compelling enough - wrong audience, weak hook, or poor creative."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"High bounce rate (above 70%) within 3 seconds:"}]," Message mismatch. Visitors are landing and immediately registering that they're in the wrong place."]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Fix the correct layer first. Improving a landing page won't help if the ad isn't generating clicks. Improving the ad won't help if the landing page destroys the trust the ad built."}]]}]
a:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Quick Fixes for Meta Landing Pages"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Once you've confirmed the page is the leak, these are the highest-priority changes to implement first - roughly ordered by effort-to-priority ratio."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Match the hero image style to the ad creative."}]," If the ad showed a real person in a casual setting, the landing page should open with the same visual register - not a polished studio product shot."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Repeat the exact ad headline on the page."}]," Don't make the visitor re-orient. The first thing they read should echo the reason they clicked."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Add proof before the form."}]," A minimum of one testimonial with a name, photo, and specific result should appear above or immediately adjacent to the form. Generic five-star ratings without context don't count."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Reduce form fields."}]," Every additional field reduces conversion rate. For cold Meta traffic, ask for the minimum: name and email. Qualify further via follow-up, not the form itself."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-accent font-bold","children":"→"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Rewrite the button copy."}]," 'Submit' or 'Sign up' does not explain the next step. Test a specific label such as 'Send me the guide' against the current control."]}]]}]]}]]}]
b:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-accent/40 bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Find the leak on your page"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Run the free Nebula audit to see exactly where your page breaks the chain from click to conversion."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-4","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre&utm_medium=organic-content","className":"inline-flex rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-bg hover:opacity-85 hover:bg-accent transition-colors","children":"Run the free audit"}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/paid-traffic-leak-map","className":"inline-flex rounded border border-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-accent hover:bg-accent-dim transition-colors","children":"Open leak map"}]]}]]}]
